  "audio": null,
  "verify": "Pins from Waveshare's demo code and schematic (https://github.com/waveshareteam/ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.64-v2). Two hardware revisions with different pins; this is V1.1 (Rev1.1 on the schematic, version silkscreen on the right side of the PCB by the pin headers), whose examples are the GitHub repository named -v2. V1 (silkscreen at the top; record esp32-s3-touch-amoled-1.64) has the panel's CS on GPIO9 and the IMU's INT1 on GPIO46, and leaves TE, the touch interrupt, the touch reset and IMU INT2 unconnected. The glass has rounded corners whose radius Waveshare does not give, so the designer draws them square: keep what matters out of the corners, or set a corner radius on the Display tab once it is measured. Brightness is a command to the panel, not a backlight pin. Compiled; not run on a board here.",
